    "registry_text": "Inclusion Criteria:\n\nAdults aged 18 years or older, regardless of sex.\n\nConfirmed Chlamydia trachomatis and/or Neisseria gonorrhoeae infection diagnosed by nucleic acid amplification testing (NAAT/PCR) or culture at the Centre Hospitalier de Martigues.\n\nSymptomatic or asymptomatic individuals receiving medical care for a sexually transmitted infection.\n\nNo antibiotic treatment targeting Chlamydia trachomatis or Neisseria gonorrhoeae within the 7 days preceding enrollment.\n\nIndividuals who have received written and oral information about the study and have provided free, informed, written consent after an appropriate reflection period.\n\nIndividuals agreeing to attend the scheduled follow-up visits.\n\nIndividuals able to read, understand, and complete the study questionnaires in French, including the KABP questionnaire.\n\nIndividuals accepting the specific research procedures in accordance with applicable regulations.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Individuals younger than 18 years.\n\nAbsence of microbiological confirmation of Chlamydia trachomatis and/or Neisseria gonorrhoeae infection by NAAT/PCR or culture.\n\nAntibiotic treatment targeting Chlamydia trachomatis or Neisseria gonorrhoeae initiated before enrollment.\n\nIndividuals deprived of liberty by judicial or administrative decision.\n\nIndividuals under legal protection measures (guardianship, curatorship, or judicial protection) or otherwise unable to provide informed consent, in accordance with the study protocol.\n\nIndividuals who do not sufficiently understand French to receive study information or complete the questionnaires.\n\nIndividuals unable to comply with the scheduled follow-up visits or study-specific procedures.\n\nIndividuals who refuse to participate or decline to sign the informed consent form.\n\nIndividuals participating in another interventional study that may interfere with the objectives of ECART-IST.\n\nIndividuals whose medical condition or situation